---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaSection from '../../components/CtaSection.astro';
import { graph, breadcrumbs, reviewSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import { EMAIL, BOILERPLATE } from '../../data/site';

const jsonLd = graph(
  breadcrumbs([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Case Studies', path: '/case-studies' },
    { name: 'EdTech workforce training', path: '/case-studies/edtech-workforce-training' },
  ]),
  reviewSchema({
    body: "You have done such a great job that I can't remember how we were working before you.",
    authorName: 'CEO',
    authorTitle: 'EdTech workforce-training company',
  })
);

const metrics = [
  { value: 'Zero → daily', label: 'From zero operational visibility to fully automated daily reporting.' },
  { value: '30–40 → 12–16', label: 'Applicants to accepted, every stage tracked.' },
  { value: 'Sunday, every week', label: 'At-risk stipend alerts to participant and coach, before the problem lands.' },
];

const stack = [
  'Airtable',
  'OpenAI',
  'Read.ai',
  'Supabase',
  'SendGrid',
  'Microsoft Power Automate',
  'SharePoint',
  'Gmail',
];
---
<Base
  title="EdTech workforce training: Six Connected Systems | pocho.tech"
  description="Six connected systems run admissions and operations at an EdTech workforce-training company: AI-scored interviews, stipend alerts, daily reports. Built by Erick Bonilla."
  path="/case-studies/edtech-workforce-training"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="cs-header">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>EdTech workforce training</h1>
      <p class="client-line"><strong>Clean-tech workforce training, Boston.</strong> Runs an 8-week, stipend-based training program for immigrants and minorities. 30–40 applicants per cohort; 12–16 accepted. Six systems in production, built as an embedded team member.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The before</h2>
      <div class="before-block">
        <p>Every cohort starts with 30 to 40 applications and ends with 12 to 16 seats. Between those two numbers: intake forms, interviews, scoring, scheduling emails, stipend rules, and a team holding it together by hand.</p>
        <p>There was no operational visibility. Nobody could see, in one place, where a candidate stood, which interviews had been evaluated, or who was at risk of losing stipend eligibility.</p>
        <p>The stipend part carried the most weight. Eligibility data sat in SharePoint, invisible to the participant and coach who needed the warning.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What I built</h2>
      <p>Six connected systems, running as one operation.</p>
      <ol class="systems">
        <li><strong>Airtable ATS</strong>: Intake forms feed one applicant pipeline, so every candidate has a single record and a visible stage from application to acceptance.</li>
        <li><strong>AI interview evaluation</strong>: A Read.ai transcript webhook matches the candidate, applies objective scoring, runs an AI qualitative evaluation with direct quotes from the interview, and delivers a structured brief to the human reviewers.</li>
        <li><strong>Interview scheduling</strong>: Scheduling emails go out automatically as candidates advance through the pipeline.</li>
        <li><strong>Daily and executive reporting</strong>: A 5pm report to the team every day, and a Monday executive summary for the CEO: week-over-week movement, demographics, bottleneck alerts.</li>
        <li><strong>Stipend eligibility notifications</strong>: SharePoint data flows through Power Automate into Supabase; every Sunday, at-risk participants and their coach get an alert.</li>
        <li><strong>Real-time dashboards</strong>: Live views of the pipeline and program operations.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="systems-note">The AI doesn't decide who gets in. It reads, scores, and prepares the brief. The human reviewers make the call.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt numbers">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The numbers</h2>
      <div class="metric-grid">
        {metrics.map((m) => (
          <div class="metric-item">
            <span class="metric">{m.value}</span>
            <span class="metric-label">{m.label}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What the CEO says</h2>
      <blockquote>
        <p>"You have done such a great job that I can't remember how we were working before you."</p>
        <cite>CEO, EdTech workforce-training company</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The stack</h2>
      <ul class="stack-row">
        {stack.map((tool) => <li class="pill">{tool}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <aside class="how-started">
        <h2>How it started</h2>
        <p>A single build, then embedded work inside the team. One system became six as each bottleneck surfaced.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSection
    heading="If your program runs on forms, interviews, and deadlines"
    body="Sixty minutes: you walk me through how applicants or clients move through your operation, and I tell you what I'd automate first and what it would cost."
    secondaryLabel={EMAIL}
    secondaryHref={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="boilerplate">{BOILERPLATE}</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .cs-header { padding-block: var(--space-section) clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px); }
  .client-line { color: var(--c-text-mute); max-width: 70ch; margin-top: 16px; }
  .client-line strong { color: var(--c-text); }

  .cs-block { padding-block: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px); }

  .before-block {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--c-border);
    padding-left: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
    margin-left: 8px;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .before-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .systems {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: sys;
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .systems li {
    counter-increment: sys;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 56px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .systems li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .systems li::before {
    content: counter(sys, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 3px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--c-text-dim);
  }
  .systems strong { color: var(--c-text); }
  .systems-note {
    margin-top: 28px;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .numbers { padding-block: var(--space-section); }
  .metric-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 40px 36px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .metric {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--c-red);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .metric-label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: 36ch;
  }

  blockquote {
    background: var(--c-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 28px 32px;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  blockquote p {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--c-text);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  blockquote cite {
    display: block;
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
  }

  .stack-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .pill {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 7px 16px;
  }

  .how-started h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--c-text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .how-started p {
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .boilerplate {
    color: var(--c-text-dim);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 40px 0 0;
    max-width: 75ch;
  }
</style>
